#{[17592186511546 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511546 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123634" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511546 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511546 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }\\,$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511546 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b688c283-ffe1-5279-a25b-e224f4238243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511546 #edb/ref 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2{e}^{2\\theta }+2{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{4{e}^{2\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}2{e}^{\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\theta }{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =2({e}^{\\pi /2}-{e}^{\\pi /4}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\pi /4}({e}^{\\pi /4}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511593 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511593 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "19f4932e-c75d-5c67-b1d4-b8ff2197751a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511593 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186259520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511645 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511645 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9df4f53a-cfc3-5f5d-9dd3-d0e7ba431674" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511645 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186259519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511657 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b40a5a22-c678-5bc6-8e83-8d3a7d00ab97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511657 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511661 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511661 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ca26c44a-47b3-5082-aab1-eac96843df54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511661 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511675 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511675 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e9a0c7e4-f9f1-5b84-a2be-688ec5da197a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511675 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511541 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
